add(m,'Culture & History','09 · Medical texts & historical evidence','Sushruta and Charaka: distinguish textual heritage from modern validation','The issue revisited the medical traditions associated with the two figures.','The Sushruta tradition is associated particularly with surgery.|The Charaka tradition is associated particularly with internal medicine.|The transmitted texts have complex histories of composition and redaction.',
'Historical description of a procedure or remedy is not contemporary clinical evidence of efficacy and safety.',
'Critical scholarship can value medical heritage without anachronistic institutional claims.|Modern healthcare requires appropriate testing, ethics and qualified practice.',
'Do not present legendary chronology as certain, claim an ancient modern-style Benares University appointment, or use historical recipes as treatment advice.','How can scientific temper coexist with careful appreciation of medical heritage?',priority='P2',slug='sushruta-and-charaka')
